'''Hanimaadhoo International Airport''' ({{langx|dv|ހަނިމާދޫ ބައިނަލްއަޤުވާމީ ވައިގެ ބަނދަރު}} {{airport codes|HAQ|VRMH|p=n}}) is an [[airport]] located on the island of [[Hanimaadhoo]]<ref name="WAD">{{usurped|1={{Deprecated archive|url=https://archive.today/20130217022002/http://www.worldaerodata.com/wad.cgi?airport=VRMH|title=Airport information for VRMH}}}} from [[DAFIF]] (effective October 2006)</ref> in [[Haa Dhaalu Atoll]], [[Maldives]], opened as a domestic airport. It was upgraded to an international airport on 2 February 2012, with the introduction of direct flights to [[Thiruvananthapuram]] in [[India]] by [[Maldivian (airline)|Maldivian]].<ref>[http://www.haveeru.com.mv/dhivehi/news/133735 Haveeru News Article] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130205055405/http://www.haveeru.com.mv/dhivehi/news/133735 |date=2013-02-05 }} {{in lang|dv}}</ref> As of June 2019, it is one of three international airports in the Maldives.

[[File:Hanimaadhoo Airport.jpg |thumb| Hanimaadhoo Airport in 2014]]

==Facilities==
The airport is at an [[elevation]] of {{convert|3|ft|0}} above [[mean sea level]]. It has one [[runway]] designated 03/21 with an [[Asphalt concrete|asphalt]] surface measuring {{convert|1220|x|30|m|0}}.<ref name="WAD" /> A huge airport expansion project was announced in 2021 with the line of credit facility from [[Export-import Bank Of India|Export Import Bank of India]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hanimaadhoo Airport expansion to include development of seaplane terminal |url=https://psmnews.mv/en/83981 |access-date=2022-07-11 |website=PSMnews.mv |date=31 March 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

